@startuml
title Vertical Representation And Storage Contract
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 180
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

rectangle "Topography\nz_top(x, y)" as Top
rectangle "Layer 1\nsame planar footprint\nhead h solved in cell" as L1
rectangle "Layer 2 .. n-1\nsame planar footprint\nproperties may vary with depth" as L2
rectangle "Bottom layer\nsame planar footprint" as Ln
rectangle "Substratum\nz_bot(x, y)" as Bot

Top --> L1 : local thickness\nz_top - z_bot
L1 --> L2 : shared vertical proportions p_l
L2 --> Ln : repeated planar connectivity
Ln --> Bot

note right of L1
Geometry contract:
- one planar support reused at every layer
- top and bottom vary from cell to cell
end note

note right of L2
Geology is often represented by
layer-wise properties rather than by
independent internal interfaces.
end note

note right of Ln
Storage law stays separate from geometry:
- Sy for drainable storage
- Ss for compressive storage
end note
@enduml
